{{!-- A help mark: a drawn ring round an ink `?`, which explains the thing beside it in a tooltip.
      Core raises the tooltip from this element and localizes `tip` itself, so the key is passed,
      not its text. The ring is inked on the upper layer (`data-ink-layer="over"`) because the mark
      has an opaque paper ground and a ring under it would lose its inner half; the ground is what
      keeps it legible over a flooded box. Set it BESIDE a `<label>`, never inside one: a label
      forwards its clicks, and a click on the mark would toggle the switch it names.

      @param tip    the i18n key of the explanation
      @param label  the localized accessible name, "What … is for"
      @param seed   a stable key for this mark's ring --}}
<span class="cairn-help" role="img" data-tooltip="{{tip}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP" aria-label="{{label}}"
    data-ink="circle" data-ink-seed="help-{{seed}}" data-ink-w="1.3" data-ink-layer="over">?</span>
